{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>לאליעזר לאריאל</b> — they were the ones sent on that day. The lamed indicates the substance [i.e., the persons themselves], and its sense is: to the persons of Eliezer and those mentioned." "<b>מבינים</b> — sages."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The argument turns on the prefixed lamed (ל) marking the entity/person itself rather than direction or possession; 'substance' renders עצם in its grammatical sense."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:14.631742303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}